  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Montana federal contract obligations are $53.7M for FY2027 to date. Obligations are down 96.1% year over year. Award count in the state is 424, and average award size is $127K. Fiscal-year comparisons show recent peak activity: FY22 obligations were $925M, FY23 were $1B, FY24 were $1.1B, FY25 were $1.1B, and FY26 were $1.4B. The Department of the Interior is the largest buyer so far in FY2027 to date at $28.6M, followed by the Department of Agriculture at $12.4M and the Department of Health and Human Services at $6.1M. Construction, air transportation, and outpatient care dominate industry-level obligations, with Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $21.9M and Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation at $6.8M. PAULSEN CONSTRUCTION LLC is the largest vendor at $21.6M. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How do FY2027 to date obligations compare with recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "Montana obligations for FY2027 to date are $53.7M. Recent fiscal years were much larger: FY22 was $925M, FY23 was $1B, FY24 was $1.1B, FY25 was $1.1B, and FY26 was $1.4B. Obligations are down 96.1% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and industries account for most FY2027 to date spending in Montana?",
        "body": "The Department of the Interior leads buying in FY2027 to date at $28.6M, followed by the Department of Agriculture at $12.4M and the Department of Health and Human Services at $6.1M. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is the largest industry at $21.9M, with Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation at $6.8M and All Other Outpatient Care Centers at $6.7M."
      }
    ]
  },
